## EWG's Guide to Healthy Cleaning (Household Products)

- [Guide to Healthy Cleaning Portal](https://www.ewg.org/cleaners/): Main search index and database grading 2,000+ household cleaning products, detergents, and laundry supplies on an A-to-F scale.
- [Scoring Framework & Methodology](https://www.ewg.org/cleaners/content/methodology/): Core scientific documentation detailing the three-step logic system (Information collection, Endpoint mapping, and Assessment tier weighting) used to assign product grades.
- [Product & Ingredient Sourcing Architecture](https://www.ewg.org/cleaners/content/ingredients/): Technical breakdown of how ingredient data is compiled from labels, worker safety sheets, and 15 regulatory/academic toxicity datasets.
- [Label Decoder Reference](https://www.ewg.org/cleaners/content/decode/): A textual key defining deceptive marketing buzzwords (e.g., "biodegradable," "chlorine-free") and clarifying how they align with actual chemical formulations.
- [Core Scientific Findings Report](https://www.ewg.org/cleaners/content/cleaner-findings/): A flat text summary mapping structural hazards found during extensive testing, including formaldehyde and quaternary ammonium compounds.
- [Cleaning Chemical Health Risks Guide](https://www.ewg.org/cleaners/content/health-risks/): Comprehensive safety indices addressing systemic health concerns, detailing asthma induction risks, chemical burns, and developmental toxicity.

## EWG's Food Scores Database

- [EWG's Food Scores Hub](https://www.ewg.org/foodscores/): Search portal for a database of 80,000+ packaged foods rated on a 1 (healthiest) to 10 (least healthy) scale.
- [Overall Score Calculation Methodology](https://www.ewg.org/foodscores/content/methodology-overall/): Mathematical breakdown of how nutrition, ingredient concerns, and degree of processing are weighted and compiled into a single unified score.
- [Nutrition Scoring Algorithm](https://www.ewg.org/foodscores/content/methodology-nutrition/): Detailed framework based on the UK Ofcom/Oxford profiling model, highlighting how EWG calculates penalties for added sugars, trans fats, and synthetic sweeteners.
- [Ingredient & Additive Assessment Framework](https://www.ewg.org/foodscores/content/methodology-ingredients/): Technical documentation regarding the weight-of-evidence calculation for food contaminants, heavy metals, pesticides, and chemical food additives.
- [Food Scores User Guide](https://www.ewg.org/foodscores/content/user-guide/): Explains database constraints, product tracking via the Healthy Living barcode scanner app, and personalized nutritional tailoring.

