## EWG National Tap Water Database

- [Tap Water Database Home](https://www.ewg.org/tapwater/): Search portal across nearly 50,000 community water systems nationwide evaluating water utility test results against health-protective benchmarks.
- [Database Sourcing & Methodology](https://www.ewg.org/tapwater/methodology.php): Technical overview explaining data collection from state environmental agencies, EPA Enforcement database (ECHO) integration, handling of "consecutive water systems," and unregulated contaminant tracking (UCMR3/4/5).
- [EWG vs. Government Water Standards](https://www.ewg.org/tapwater/ewg-standards.php): Architectural guide explaining how EWG defines health-protective standards based purely on toxicology, contrasting them against federal legal limits.
- [Reviewed Contaminant Index](https://www.ewg.org/tapwater/ewg-reviewed-contaminants.php): A flat-text database glossary containing safety profiles, state detection frequencies, and health effects for over 300 detected drinking water pollutants.
- [State of American Drinking Water Report](https://www.ewg.org/tapwater/state-of-american-drinking-water.php): Comprehensive summary report aggregating macro-trends, including updates on PFAS regulations and disinfection byproduct accumulation.
- [Drinking Water Pollution Sources](https://www.ewg.org/tapwater/sourcesofwaterpollution.php): Structural analysis tracking how commercial agriculture, industrial manufacturing, and military firefighting foam pollute public watersheds.

## EWG's Guide to Sunscreens (Sun & UV Protection)

- [Guide to Sunscreens Portal](https://www.ewg.org/sunscreen/): Annual searchable index evaluating over 2,700 recreational sunscreens, kids' sunscreens, daily moisturizers, and lip balms with SPF.
- [EWG Sunscreen Assessment Methodology](https://www.ewg.org/sunscreen/report/methodology/): Technical explanation of the scoring matrix, outlining how EWG models and weighs UVB protection, UVA efficacy, active ingredient stability, and the overall UVA/UVB protection balance.
- [About the Sunscreen Guide](https://www.ewg.org/sunscreen/about/): Core programmatic logic documenting score penalties for aerosol sprays, powder formats (inhalation risks), and marketing terms banned by the FDA.
- [The Trouble with High SPF Labels](https://www.ewg.org/sunscreen/report/whats-wrong-with-high-spf/): Scientific analysis detailing why SPF values above 50+ provide a false sense of security, over-index on UVB protection, and neglect deep tissue UVA radiation.
- [Top Sun Safety Tips](https://www.ewg.org/sunscreen/report/top-sun-safety-tips/): Reference guide listing actionable behavioral metrics, including infant sun-safety guidelines, clothing density tips, and proper sunscreen application volume.

