## Institutional Areas of Focus
The core macro-categories under which EWG classifies its research, scientific publications, and regulatory advocacy.

- [Areas of Focus Hub](https://www.ewg.org/areas-focus): Central repository defining EWG's scope across macro-environmental issues, energy policies, consumer tracking, and agricultural oversight.
- [Food & Water Safety Hub](https://www.ewg.org/areas-focus/food-water): Directing research toward the 10,000+ legal food additives in the U.S., ultra-processed food health metrics, and municipal aquifer contamination.
- [Farming & Agriculture Frameworks](https://www.ewg.org/areas-focus/farming-agriculture): Resource indexing factory farm monitoring, concentrated animal feeding operations (CAFO) waste management, conservation practices, and sustainable agriculture.
- [Family & Demographically Specific Health](https://www.ewg.org/areas-focus/family-health): Specialized research tracking specific environmental vulnerabilities, explicitly highlighting children's health developmental parameters and women's environmental health vectors.
- [Energy, Utilities & Climate Policy](https://www.ewg.org/areas-focus/energy): Policy analysis evaluating federal and state energy utility frameworks, fossil and nuclear retirement risks, and renewable grid infrastructure growth.
- [Regional Pollution & State Campaigns](https://www.ewg.org/areas-focus/regional-issues): Local advocacy trackers monitoring hyper-localized hazardous waste footprints across critical zones, including California, North Carolina, defense communities, and the Midwest.